  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CCI core support II phase</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CCI core support II phase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The vision of CCI is: Citizens in BiH understand and participate in developing democratic processes and civil society. 

The mission of CCI is: To enable Bosnia and Herzegovina&apos;s citizens to achieve their interests and increase influence in the decision-making process. 

The strategy of CCI focuses on five different areas:

1) Good governance and citizen participation: Established transparent, responsible, depoliticized, and efficient public administration that responds to citizens&apos; needs and engages citizens in decision-making.

2) Countering corruption and misuse of public resources: BiH society establishes a zero-tolerance rate for all forms of corruption and misuse of public resources.

3) The rule of law and election processes: The improved rule of law in BiH and restored citizens&apos; confidence in the electoral process.

4) EU integrations: State institutions, with the active involvement of civil society, have taken essential steps and reforms in areas important for the accession to the European Union.

5) Sustainable civil society: Improved perspectives for the sustainability of civil society organizations in BiH.

CCI detailed the actions it takes in each of the strategic areas.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Detta &#xe4;r forts&#xe4;ttningen p&#xe5; det strategiska partnerskapet som ges genom k&#xe4;rnfinansiering. CCI:s strategi har fem prioriteringar vilket &#xe4;r f&#xf6;ljande: (1) god f&#xf6;rvaltning och medborgardeltagande; (2) motverka korruption och missbruk av offentliga resurser; (3) r&#xe4;ttsstaten och valprocesser; (4) EU-integration samt; (5) h&#xe5;llbart civilt samh&#xe4;lle. Det bed&#xf6;ms att k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;det till CCI &#xe4;r i linje med strategin f&#xf6;r Sveriges reformsamarbete med v&#xe4;stra Balkan och Turkiet 2021&#x2013;2027. K&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;det kommer huvudsakligen omfatta omr&#xe5;dena m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter, demokrati, r&#xe4;ttsstatsprincipen och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och kommer innefatta f&#xf6;ljande m&#xe5;l: f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad demokratisk samh&#xe4;llsstyrning och &#xf6;kad respekt f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter och r&#xe4;ttsstatsprincipen, f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade villkor f&#xf6;r ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande, &#xf6;kad transparens och minskad korruption. K&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;det bidrar &#xe4;ven till FN:s m&#xe5;l f&#xf6;r h&#xe5;llbar utveckling, s&#xe4;rskilt SDG 16. Bidraget har &#xe4;ven ett starkt samband till vad som kr&#xe4;vs f&#xf6;r att inleda f&#xf6;rhandlingar om anslutning till EU. I sitt yttrande om Bosnien och Hercegovinas ans&#xf6;kan om EU-medlemskap, fastst&#xe4;llde Europeiska kommissionen 14 nyckelprioriteringar f&#xf6;r att inleda anslutningsf&#xf6;rhandlingar. Denna insats kan framf&#xf6;r allt relateras till prioritering 1, 7, 11 och 14.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is the continuation of the strategic partnership through core funding support. CCI&#xb4;s strategy has five strategic priorities: Strategic area 1: Good governance and citizen participation, Strategic area 2: Countering corruption and misuse of public resources, Strategic area 3: The Rule of Law and Election Processes, Strategic area 4: EU integrations, Strategic area 5: Sustainable Civil Society. The contribution to CCI in the form of core support is assessed as aligned with the Strategy for Sweden&apos;s reform cooperation with the Western Balkans and Turkey for 2021&#x2013;2027. The main contribution of this core support is expected to be in the result area Human rights, democracy, the rule of law, and gender equality, with the following objectives: Better democratic governance and greater respect for human rights and the rule of law, and Improved conditions for accountability, increased transparency, and reduced corruption. This core support also contributes to the UN Sustainable Development Goals, specifically SDG 16. Finally, this contribution is strongly related to the EU accession negotiations. To open negotiations, BiH must implement 14 key priorities set out in the European Commission&apos;s opinion. This contribution is especially related to the priorities 1, 7, 11, and 14.</narrative>
  </description>
